$$
\begin{align}
\frac{11x}{11}&=\frac{33}{11} \\
\therefore x&=3
\end{align}
$$

Checking:

$$
\begin{align}
11(3)&=33 \\
33&=33 \\
\therefore \text{LHS}&=\text{RHS}
\end{align}
$$

$$
\begin{align}
18-18+p&=6-18 \\
\therefore p&=-12 \\
\end{align}
$$

Checking:

$$
\begin{align}
18+(-12)&=6 \\
6&=6 \\
\therefore \text{LHS}&=\text{RHS}
\end{align}
$$

$$
\begin{align}
\frac{4}{1}\times \frac{1}{4}y&=\frac{4}{1}\times5 \\
y&=\frac{4\times5}{1} \\
\therefore y&=20
\end{align}
$$

Checking:

$$
\begin{align}
\frac{1}{4}(20)&=5 \\
\frac{1\times 20}{4}&=5 \\
5&=5 \\
\therefore \text{LHS}&=\text{RHS}
\end{align}
$$
